G0166.def:
αἰώνιος, -ον (as usual in Attic), also -α, -ον. 2 Thessaloniciens 2:16, Hébreux 9:12; 
(αἰών), [in LXX chiefly for עוֹלָם ;] 
age-long, eternal, 
__(a) of that which is without either beginning or end: Romains 16:26, Hébreux 9:14; 
__(b) of that which is without beginning: Romains 16:25, 2 Timothée 1:9, Tite 1:2; 
__(with) of that which is without end (MM, VGT, see word): σκηναί, Luc 16:9 οἰκία, 2 Corinthiens 5:1; διαθήκη, Hébreux 13:20; εὐαγγέλιον, Apocalypse 14:6; παράκλησις, 2 Thessaloniciens 2:16; λύτρωσις, Hébreux 9:12; κληρονομία, ib. 15; κόλασις, Matthieu 25:46; κρίμα, Hébreux 6:2; κρίσις, Marc 3:29; ὄλεθρον, 2 Thessaloniciens 1:9; πῦρ, Matthieu 18:8; frequently with ζωή, which see 
SYN.: ἀΐδιος, which see

G0169.def:
ἀκάθαρτος, -ον 
(ἀ- neg., καθαίρω), [in LXX chiefly for טָמֵא ;] 
unclean, impure; 
__(a) physically (LS, MM, VGT, see word);
__(b) ceremonially: Actes 10:14,28 11:8, 1 Corinthiens 7:14, 2 Corinthiens 6:17, Apocalypse 18:2; 
__(with) morally: Éphésiens 5:5, Apocalypse 17:4; with πνεῦμα, as always in Gosp., Matthieu 10:1 12:43, Marc 1:23,26,27 3:11,30 5:2,8,13 6:7 7:25 9:25, Luc 4:33,36 6:18 8:29 9:42 11:24, Actes 5:16 8:7, Apocalypse 16:13 (cf. Cremer, 320). 
